            <ArticleTitle>[Efficacy of diclofenac continuous perfusion in hyperalgic bone metastases. Apropos of 20 cases treated at Gustave Roussy Institute].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>571-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this trial, 20 patients suffering from bone metastasis pain received diclofenac, a non-steroid anti-inflammatory agent, by continuous IV infusion. No pain was observed in 77% after 2.7 days of treatment. 33% of bedridden patients were able to move again. Two patients (10%) presented gastric pain controlled by symptomatic treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
